<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n16017" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀρχι-τέκτων</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ονος</span>,
			ὁ, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>chief-artificer, master-builder, director of works,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ ὀρύγματος, τῆς γεφύρας,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hdt.
				3.60
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				4.87
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">χειροτέχνης,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Metaph.</u>
				981a30
			</span></i>; opp. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐργατικός,</span>
			<i><span class="en">
				Pl.
				<u>Plt.</u>
				259e
			</span></i>; <i>commissioner of works,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				IG
				2.403
			</span></i>, al., ib.<i><span class="en">
				9(1).694.145
			</span></i> (<span class="entity">Corcyra</span>), <i><span class="en">
				<u>SIG</u>
				284.12
			</span></i> (Chios, from Erythrae), etc.; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τοῦ
				ναοῦ</span> ib.<i><span class="en">
				494.3
			</span></i> (Delph.); 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. ἐπὶ τὰ ἱερά</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					<u>IG</u>
					2.404
				</span></i>
			. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense4"><b>b.</b> pl., <i>board
				of naval constructors,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Arist.
				<u>Ath.</u>
				46.1
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense3"><b>2.</b> generally,
				<i>author, contriver,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				E.
				<u>Cyc.</u>
				477
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. κύριος τῆς ἡδονῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Alex.
					149.2
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀ. τῆς ἐπιβουλῆς</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					D.
					56.11
				</span></i>
			; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοῦ τέλους</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Arist.
					<u>EN</u>
					1152b2
				</span></i>
			; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τοὺς ταῖς διανοίαις ἀ. τινός</span>
			<i>those that direct activities</i> by thought, <i><span class="en">
				Id.
				<u>Pol.</u>
				1325b23
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b> at Athens,
				<i>manager of the state theatre and of the Dionysia,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				D.
				18.28
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>IG</u>
				2.335
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
